{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And it was on the third day, when they were in pain.</b> All of them were suffering and regretting that they had circumcised. And the sons of Jacob heard and knew that Hamor and Shechem had changed the condition, and had addressed the men of their city, and pinned the honor on the men of the city and not on Jacob and his household. Moreover, Hamor and Shechem had said: 'their acquirements and possessions and all their livestock — are they not ours?' Therefore 'they came upon the city,' etc. And why on the third day? Because in one day the men of the city would not have enough time to circumcise, nor even in two; and on the third they finished circumcising, and all were in pain and wounded then, so 'they came upon the city safely' — and so Targum Onkelos. Another interpretation: <b>upon</b> the men <b>of the city</b> who were sitting <b>safely</b> — they did not take precautions against them." "<b>And they killed every male.</b> Because the children of Noah are commanded to establish a court in every district, and they saw that he had seized Dinah and they did not bring him to judgment."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:22.103956242Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}